      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "ign",
        "memory_description": "The IGN website has inconsistent UI element placement and ambiguous interaction cues, leading to task failure.",
        "content_body": "On the IGN website, UI layout pitfalls include unexpected placement of category filters and review scores, making it difficult to locate the correct elements. For example, the 'boardgame' category filter was not where expected, and the '10' score filter was mislabeled or mispositioned. Interaction traps include case-sensitivity in dropdown selections (e.g., 'board' vs. 'Board') and inconsistent element IDs, which caused incorrect selections. To succeed, users should carefully check the exact labels and case of dropdown options and verify the position of filters relative to the review listings."
      }
