      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "rottentomatoes",
        "memory_description": "Rotten Tomatoes website has inconsistent element positioning and unclear navigation for accessing TV content.",
        "content_body": "On Rotten Tomatoes, the UI layout pitfalls include unexpected element positions, such as the 'Most Popular TV' section not being in a predictable location, which can confuse automated navigation. Additionally, the website interaction traps involve requiring users to click on a specific, non-obvious element (e.g., a hidden or dynamically loaded section) to access the full list of Most Popular TV shows, rather than using a direct navigation link. Correct interaction involves locating and clicking the specific element that triggers the full list, which may not be immediately visible or intuitive."
      }
