        "scenario_description": "ikea",
        "memory_description": "IKEA website has dynamic UI elements and inconsistent interaction patterns that lead to task failure.",
        "content_body": "On the IKEA website, UI layout pitfalls include dynamically loaded store locators and unclear selection states, which can mislead users about available options. Interaction traps involve unexpected element IDs and non-intuitive actions, such as requiring multiple clicks to select a store and navigate to its page. Users may fail to recognize that selecting a store location requires a separate confirmation step before accessing store-specific details, and the correct interaction involves clicking the 'Select' button after searching, followed by navigating to the store page through a dedicated link or button."
      }
    },
