      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "menards",
        "memory_description": "Menards website has dynamic content loading and inconsistent UI element positioning, leading to interaction failures.",
        "content_body": "On the Menards website, UI layout pitfalls include dynamically loaded content and non-static element positions, which can cause elements to shift or not appear as expected. For the task of adding a pre-made College Supply List to your list, the first step failed due to the absence of the target element in the cleaned HTML, likely because the content was not fully loaded or rendered. Website interaction traps involve relying on static element IDs or positions, which can change dynamically. The correct interaction is to wait for full page load and use dynamic selectors or check for content readiness before attempting to click on elements."
      }
