      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "yellowpages",
        "memory_description": "Yellowpages website has inconsistent UI layout and unclear interaction pathways for filtering services.",
        "content_body": "On the Yellowpages website, UI layout pitfalls include unexpected placement of search filters and dynamic element IDs that change between pages, making it difficult to reliably select the correct elements. Website interaction traps involve incorrect click targets for filtering options (e.g., clicking on 'Attorney' categories without properly navigating to the filtering panel), as well as inconsistent input handling for location searches (e.g., expecting 'West Hollywood, Florida' but the system only accepts 'west hollywood' without state). Correct interaction requires navigating to the 'Attorney' category first, then using the filtering panel to apply criteria like 'drug charges,' 'credit cards,' and 'Spanish' language, while ensuring location input matches the site's expected format."
      }
    },
