      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "cvs",
        "memory_description": "CVS website has dynamic UI elements and inconsistent form field labels, leading to interaction and layout pitfalls.",
        "content_body": "On the CVS website, UI layout pitfalls include elements not being in expected locations, such as dropdowns and form fields appearing in non-standard positions or being dynamically loaded, which caused incorrect selections. Additionally, interaction traps include mismatched form field expectations, such as selecting 'ca' instead of clicking a specific state option, typing incorrect address formats (e.g., '123 Main St' vs. '123 st'), and selecting 'ny' instead of 'New York' for state selection. These issues highlight the need for precise element targeting and strict adherence to the exact expected input formats and interaction methods on the site."
      }
    },
