      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "koa",
        "memory_description": "Koa is a deals website where clicking the search button after typing a zip code is essential for finding hot deals.",
        "content_body": "A) Website UI Layout Knowledge: Koa is a deals/offer website. Key UI components include a top navigation bar with a logo and links, a prominent search box, and a 'Search' button. The search box is typically located in the center of the top navigation bar. Interactive elements such as the search button and input fields are positioned near the center of the page. The efficient interaction order for browsing hot deals involves clicking the search box, typing the zip code, and then clicking the search button. B) Website-Specific Operation Rules: The search function on Koa requires clicking the search box to focus it, then typing the zip code, and finally clicking the search button to submit the query. Directly typing into the search box without clicking it first may not work. The search button must be clicked explicitly after entering the zip code. Element IDs such as [11789] for the search box and [19802] for the search button are consistent across the site and can be used to identify key elements. A common pitfall is assuming that pressing Enter after typing the zip code will submit the search, but on Koa, the search button must be clicked for the query to execute."
      }
    },
