      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "expedia",
        "memory_description": "Expedia website has dynamic UI elements and inconsistent interaction patterns that lead to task failure.",
        "content_body": "On Expedia, UI layout pitfalls include dynamically loaded elements and non-static positioning of filters, which caused incorrect element selection during steps 9, 16, and 17. Website interaction traps involve hidden or conditional filters (e.g., private pool, bedrooms) that require navigating through additional modals or dropdowns, which were not properly accounted for in the interaction sequence. Correct interaction involves explicitly accessing the 'More Filters' option to set private pool and bedroom requirements, and ensuring date availability is selected via the calendar widget, not just a text input."
      }
