        "scenario_description": "seatgeek",
        "memory_description": "The SeatGeek website allows direct access to help pages about ticket purchasing through a two-step navigation involving a primary menu and a sub-menu item.",
        "content_body": "On the SeatGeek website, users can navigate to a help page about buying tickets by first clicking on a primary menu item (likely labeled 'Help' or 'Support') and then selecting a specific sub-menu option related to ticket purchasing. This two-step process involves precise element selection, with the first click accessing the help section and the second click targeting the specific topic. The exact element IDs used in this process (e.g., [114] and [5941]) indicate a structured and predictable layout for help navigation, which contrasts with the previously noted inconsistencies in other parts of the site."
