      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "ticketcenter",
        "memory_description": "The ticketcenter website lacks explicit price range input fields for filtering tickets, requiring users to navigate through dynamically loaded sections or use non-intuitive controls to set price bounds.",
        "content_body": "On the ticketcenter website, when searching for tickets within a specific price range, users cannot directly input price bounds using standard price range fields. Instead, they must locate and interact with dynamically loaded or hidden elements, such as dropdowns or sliders, which are not clearly labeled or accessible via typical click actions. For example, to set a price range of $200-$300, a user must first search for the event (e.g., 'Amy Grant concert'), then navigate through dynamically generated content to find and adjust price filters, which may involve clicking on non-obvious elements or using keyboard navigation. This behavior is inconsistent with standard UI expectations and can lead to task failure if not properly accounted for."
      }
    },
