      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "underarmour",
        "memory_description": "The Under Armour website uses inconsistent input field labels and action triggers for e-gift card customization, leading to misidentification of form elements.",
        "content_body": "On the Under Armour website, when adding an e-gift card to the bag, the form fields for recipient details and message are not consistently labeled or triggered by expected actions. For example, a 'TYPE' action on a field intended for the gift message may instead trigger a 'CLICK' action, or the input field for the recipient's name may be misidentified as a different form element. This inconsistency in how form elements respond to user actions (e.g., typing vs. clicking) can lead to task failures, even when the correct element is visually identified. Users must verify both the element's purpose and the correct action type (e.g., 'CLICK' vs. 'TYPE') to ensure successful completion of the e-gift card customization process."
      }
    },
