      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "gamestop",
        "memory_description": "Gamestop's product review section lacks a direct sorting option for 'best to worst', requiring users to navigate through indirect or non-obvious pathways to achieve the task.",
        "content_body": "On Gamestop's website, when attempting to view product reviews sorted from best to worst, the expected sorting option is not directly available in the review section. Instead of a visible and accessible dropdown or button labeled 'Sort by: Best to Worst', users must navigate through hidden or non-intuitive pathways, such as clicking on individual review ratings or using search filters that are not clearly labeled for this purpose. This absence of a direct sorting mechanism creates a usability gap, as users must infer or discover the correct interaction flow through trial and error, rather than through explicit UI cues."
      }
    },
