      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "tvguide",
        "memory_description": "The TV Guide website lacks a direct 'Add to Watchlist' button on show pages, requiring users to navigate through an unclear secondary menu or use a non-obvious interaction to achieve the task.",
        "content_body": "On the TV Guide website, show pages do not feature a clearly labeled 'Add to Watchlist' button. Instead, users must locate a hidden or non-intuitive menu option, often found under a 'More' or 'Options' dropdown, which is not consistently positioned across all show pages. This design choice creates confusion and increases the likelihood of task failure, as users may not recognize the need to look for such a menu or may overlook it due to inconsistent placement."
      }
    },
