        "scenario_description": "jetblue",
        "memory_description": "JetBlue's flight selection interface requires an explicit 'economy class' toggle before viewing available options, which was not previously documented.",
        "content_body": "On JetBlue's website, when booking flights, users must explicitly select the 'economy class' option from a hidden or non-obvious toggle or filter menu before the system displays available flights. This step is not always intuitive and may be overlooked, leading to failure in identifying or selecting the correct flight options. The toggle is often located in a separate section of the UI, such as under a 'class' dropdown or a 'traveler preferences' panel, and must be engaged prior to viewing or selecting flights for the booking process to proceed correctly."
      }
    },
