      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "amazon",
        "memory_description": "Amazon's search filters require explicit price range input rather than relying on auto-applied budget constraints.",
        "content_body": "On Amazon, when filtering products like wireless headphones with specific features (e.g., active noise-cancelling) and a budget limit (e.g., $100 or less), it is necessary to manually input the price range using the 'Price' filter option. Simply typing the budget into the search bar does not automatically apply the price constraint. Users must explicitly select the 'Price' filter and set the maximum value to $100 to ensure results meet the budget requirement. This step is critical for narrowing down the product list to eligible items before adding them to the cart."
      }
