      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "cabelas",
        "memory_description": "The Cabelas website dynamically changes element IDs for product filters, making it impossible to rely on static IDs for selecting 5-star rated saltwater rods.",
        "content_body": "On the Cabelas website, when searching for 5-star rated saltwater rods, the filter options for ratings and product categories are rendered with dynamically generated element IDs that change between page loads. This makes it difficult to consistently target the correct filter elements using static identifiers. Additionally, the 'saltwater rods' category may not be explicitly labeled in the navigation, requiring users to navigate through a broader 'fishing rods' section and apply filters manually. To successfully complete the task, the interaction must dynamically detect and apply the 'saltwater' and '5-star' filters in real-time, rather than relying on fixed element IDs or assumptions about the UI structure."
      }
    },
