      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "marriott",
        "memory_description": "The Marriott website's search form requires users to select hotel chains (e.g., Marriott or Sheraton) from a dropdown menu before entering location details, which is not intuitive and leads to task failure.",
        "content_body": "On the Marriott website, when searching for hotel rooms, users must first select a hotel chain (such as Marriott or Sheraton) from a dropdown menu before entering location details like city or hotel name. This step is not clearly indicated in the UI, and users may skip it, leading to incorrect or incomplete search results. The dropdown menu for hotel chains is often overlooked or hidden, making it easy to miss during the search process. This interaction rule is not intuitive and can cause task failure if users assume they can directly input location details without first selecting a hotel chain."
      }
    },
