      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "seatgeek",
        "memory_description": "The SeatGeek website has inconsistent element IDs for event-specific filters, leading to incorrect selection of date and location filters during ticket searches.",
        "content_body": "On the SeatGeek website, when searching for events with specific dates and locations, the element IDs for filters such as 'date' and 'location' are dynamically generated and inconsistent across different search sessions or pages. This makes it difficult to reliably select the correct input fields for specifying the event date (e.g., April) and location (e.g., Hamilton, New York). Users must carefully verify the exact labels and IDs of these elements during each session, as previously recorded element IDs may no longer be valid. Additionally, the system may not always display the expected location options (e.g., 'Hamilton, New York') in the dropdown, requiring users to type the exact city name as expected by the system."
      }
    },
