        "scenario_description": "carmax",
        "memory_description": "The Carmax website dynamically alters element IDs and positions during the search process, making it difficult to consistently target specific filters like exterior color and price range.",
        "content_body": "On the Carmax website, when attempting to filter vehicles by attributes such as exterior color (e.g., black) and price (e.g., maximum $30,000), the element IDs and positions of the relevant UI components (e.g., color dropdowns, price sliders) change dynamically as the user interacts with the site. This means that even if a correct element is clicked in one step, the same element may no longer be available or correctly labeled in subsequent steps. Additionally, some filters may not be directly accessible via standard interaction paths, requiring users to navigate through hidden or dynamically generated UI elements to apply the desired criteria."
      }
    },
