      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "amtrak",
        "memory_description": "The Amtrak website dynamically loads route-specific filters, causing selectors for route names and days of the week to be unavailable in initial HTML.",
        "content_body": "On the Amtrak website, when attempting to show schedules for a specific route like the Blue Water on Wednesdays, the route name and day filters are often loaded dynamically after the initial page load. This means that the relevant UI elements for selecting the route and day are not present in the initial HTML and must be explicitly waited for before interaction. Additionally, the dynamically generated element IDs and non-semantic class names make it difficult to reliably target these filters using static selectors. To successfully complete the task, ensure that the target elements for route and day selection are both visible and correctly identified in the DOM after dynamic content has fully loaded."
      }
    },
