        "scenario_description": "cabelas",
        "memory_description": "The Cabelas website dynamically changes element IDs for price range filters, making it impossible to reliably select price ranges for product searches.",
        "content_body": "On the Cabelas website, when attempting to show Life Vests priced between $100 and $200, the UI elements used to set the price range (e.g., minimum and maximum price inputs) are rendered with dynamically generated element IDs that change between page loads. This makes it impossible to consistently target the correct input fields using static identifiers. Additionally, the price filter options may not be explicitly labeled or may be nested within a broader 'price' or 'sort' section, requiring users to navigate through multiple layers of the UI to apply the filter. To successfully complete the task, the interaction must dynamically detect and apply the $100 to $200 price range filter in real-time, rather than relying on fixed element IDs or assumptions about the UI structure."
      }
    },
