      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "rei",
        "memory_description": "The website's class booking process requires filtering by location and availability through a hidden or non-standard search interface that is not accessible via typical dropdowns or text fields.",
        "content_body": "On the REI website, booking a mountain biking class within 100 miles of New York City requires navigating to a hidden or non-standard search interface, often embedded within a 'Classes' or 'Workshops' section. This interface does not use standard text fields or dropdowns for location input; instead, it may require clicking on a 'Find Classes' button or using a map-based location picker. Additionally, the availability filter is not always visible and may be nested under a 'Filters' or 'Sort' menu. Users must first select the class type (e.g., 'Mountain Biking'), then use the location filter to input 'New York City' or select a radius (e.g., '100 miles'), and finally choose an available date and time. Failure to access the correct search interface or apply the filters in the right order will result in no results being displayed or the booking process failing."
      }
    },
