      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "budget",
        "memory_description": "The website allows direct download of e-receipts by entering a last name and confirmation number in specific fields and clicking a download button.",
        "content_body": "On the Budget website, users can download an e-receipt by navigating to a dedicated receipt or transaction section. The process involves entering the customer's last name (e.g., 'Smith') into a text field and inputting the confirmation number (e.g., 'X123456989') into another text field. After correctly entering both pieces of information, a download button becomes available and must be clicked to retrieve the e-receipt. This interaction involves direct text input into clearly labeled fields followed by a click action on a visible download button, which is a distinct process from previously documented website behaviors related to car rental searches and location inputs."
      }
    },
