      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "budget",
        "memory_description": "The website requires selecting a vehicle type (e.g., SUV) from a hidden or non-intuitive filter, not directly on the search results page.",
        "content_body": "On the Budget website, when booking a car rental, users cannot directly filter search results by vehicle type (e.g., Standard SUV) on the initial search results page. Instead, they must first select a car and then navigate to a separate section or use a hidden filter option that is not clearly labeled or accessible through standard search parameters. This behavior is not intuitive and was not previously documented, leading to task failure when attempting to apply vehicle-type filters during the search process."
      }
