      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "amtrak",
        "memory_description": "The Amtrak website dynamically loads passenger information fields, causing selectors for name entry and assistance needs to be unavailable in initial HTML.",
        "content_body": "On the Amtrak website, when attempting to book a ticket for a passenger with specific needs such as requiring assistance or carrying a bike, the passenger information fields (e.g., name entry, assistance request, bike indication) are often loaded dynamically after the initial page load. This means that the relevant UI elements for entering passenger details are not present in the initial HTML and must be explicitly waited for before interaction. Additionally, the dynamically generated element IDs and non-semantic class names make it difficult to reliably target these fields using static selectors. To successfully complete the task, ensure that the target elements for passenger information are both visible and correctly identified in the DOM after dynamic content has fully loaded."
      }
    },
