      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "yellowpages",
        "memory_description": "The Yellowpages website requires explicit navigation to a 'People' or 'Directory' panel before applying address-based filters, which was not previously documented.",
        "content_body": "On the Yellowpages website, to successfully find a person by address (e.g., 'Nice st - 1234, Good, FL'), users must first navigate to the 'People' or 'Directory' panel (often labeled as 'Browse by Category' or 'Find People'). From there, they should use the filtering options within that panel to specify the address. The location input must be entered exactly as 'Nice st - 1234, Good, FL' without any additional formatting or abbreviations. This process ensures that the filtering panel is properly engaged before applying address-based criteria."
      }
    },
